PS5 GPU: clock governor, KFD TLB flush

- GPU clock governor with a temperature limit (Borchev, #66; ps5_gpufreq.temp_limit, 85 C by default), registered
  by amdgpu. rmux's devfreq ps5-gpufreq has no thermal limit and stays disabled (CONFIG_PS5_GPUFREQ).
- GPU clock after CPU boost: MP1's universal mode, entered each time a boost frequency is chosen, sets a GPU
  clock range of 2000 MHz and up. The governor's cached clock was then stale and an idle GPU stayed at 2 GHz,
  since "500 MHz" looked already set: 62 C at the desktop instead of 46 C. mp1 now tells the governor after
  entering or leaving that mode, and the next poll requests its clock again.
- Pro (Viola firmware): gpu_metrics reported as unsupported (no SMU metrics table).
- GFX1013: the MMIO PASID TLB flush for KFD from ps5-linux-patches #57 (Tertium), which rmux's tree dropped,
  with #77 (Sergey): the PS5 never programs ATC_VMID*_PASID_MAPPING, so no VMID matched and nothing was
  flushed; KFD (ROCm/HIP, OpenCL) ran on stale translations. Every KFD VMID is flushed when none maps the
  PASID. Vulkan and games don't use KFD.
---
